  "authorNotes": "Textbook: English For Today Class 1 (md transcription in Downloads/md book/C1 Eng md file), Units 3–5 = classroom instructions, questions & answers (village/city/home/classroom), rhymes (animal sounds, 'Where do you live?', family tree). The book has no grammar, so every grammar row comes from Mohammadpur papers. Reused from MP Annual 2026: paragraph 'your school', 3 word meanings, 5 pronoun sentences (turned from 'rewrite' into fill-in-the-blank to match the row type), all 5 adjectives, 5 am/is/are, 5 prepositions, 5 capitalization, all 5 rearranging, 3 animal-home questions. Word meanings: 7 of MP 2026's 10 words (Children, Think, Go away, Again, Put on, Missing, Take) do not appear in EFT Units 3–5 (most are not in the EFT book at all), so I kept only Come, Know, Student and filled the rest with Unit 3–5 words already used in other MP papers (Live, Listen, Teacher, Say, Look, Write) + 1 new (Open). Singular/plural, gender and one article item come from MP Half-yearly 2026; four article items come from a Mohammadpur 2025 Class Test file that sits in the Half-yearly 2025 folder (header says 'Class Test - 2025'). Paragraph row offers My School OR My Country (the published syllabus names both) — choose one if only one should be printed. Doubts: (1) duration not published — used 2 h 30 min like MP 2026; (2) This/That/These/Those uses '(near, one)' cues instead of pictures — the Office can switch to pictures; (3) two preposition items now need a small picture so the answer is not ambiguous; (4) names in the and/but and comma items were changed to textbook names (Rita, Mouri, Nafis, Kazi); 'Fatima', 'Sarah and Sabah', 'Mohammad' kept from MP — swap if any is a real Sylhet student."
